#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess, from its boot through its intro's first two movies and into the
# third (#151).
#
# Nothing on the way is pressed. The logo, intro\lmi.avi, plays its 280
# frames through, flips 2 to 281, with its sound; its player clears the
# screen twice after it and twice before the next, and between them main
# waits half a second. Krisalis' logo, intro\krisalis.avi, plays its 38
# frames, flips 286 to 323, with no sound, and the game holds it two seconds;
# main waits a second more. The intro, intro\intro.avi, 320x200 doubled to
# 640x400 at y 40, plays its frames from flip 328 with its sound, and the
# route ends a dozen of them in, at 3.7 billion instructions.
#
# It ends there because every gate replays a committed route twice, and the
# lead holds this title's routes to about four billion instructions a run for
# that, where the intro played whole is 8.6 billion. It does not skip the
# intro: the game's own skip is Space, after which it waits for Space to come
# up again (0x0040D220) in a loop that presents no frame, and until #215 a key
# came up only at a flip, so skipped, it waited there for ever. Now a key comes
# up at the game's own polls between flips too, and skip-krisalis.route skips
# with Space.
